    {
      "id": "1d9db857-58ef-4448-8cda-0b2f82895f71",
      "name": "Overview Sticky",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -464,
        -288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 440,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Match Japanese government subsidies to your company with jGrants, Gemini and Slack\n\n### How it works\nJapanese SMEs leave subsidies unclaimed simply because nobody reads the jGrants portal every week. This template calls the public jGrants API for currently open subsidies, splits them into individual items, and sends each one to a Basic LLM Chain with Google Gemini together with your company profile. Gemini returns a fit score, a verdict, the reasons and the concrete next steps required to apply. Every subsidy is upserted into Google Sheets by subsidy ID so nothing is duplicated across weekly runs, then a Switch routes the outcome: strong matches raise a Slack alert and a kickoff email draft, possible matches go to review, non-matches are logged silently, and unclear results are flagged.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect Google Gemini (PaLM) API, Google Sheets, Gmail and Slack. The jGrants API needs no key.\n2. In **Set Company Profile**, enter your industry, headcount, prefecture, investment plan and search keyword.\n3. Point the Sheets node at your tracker and pick your Slack channel.\n\n### Customization tips\nRun several keywords, or filter by minimum subsidy amount."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
